    {
      "id": "eb11c1-3:explanation-1",
      "type": "worked_example",
      "lo": "eb11c1-3:objective-1",
      "source_page": 15,
      "quote": "(a) 12ab^5 / 9a^3b^2 = 4b^3 / 3a^2",
      "stem": "Simplify the rational expressions (a) $\\frac{12ab^5}{9a^3b^2}$ and (b) $\\frac{x^2-4}{3x^2+7x+2}$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "answer": "$\\frac{4b^3}{3a^2}$",
          "solution": [
            "$\\frac{12ab^5}{9a^3b^2}$ with common factors cancelled (12 and 9 by 3, a and a^3, b^2 and b^5)",
            "$=\\frac{4b^3}{3a^2}$"
          ],
          "solution_provenance": "book_worked"
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "answer": "$\\frac{x-2}{3x+1}$",
          "solution": [
            "$\\frac{x^2-4}{3x^2+7x+2}$ (note: Factorise.)",
            "$=\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{(3x+1)(x+2)}$ (note: Cancel the common factor $(x+2)$.)",
            "$=\\frac{x-2}{3x+1}$"
          ],
          "solution_provenance": "book_worked"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Explanation of Warm Up 1; the side notes are printed in margin boxes beside the steps. In (a) the cancellation is drawn as strikes with small numbers (4, 3, 3, 2, 5) read from the image; verify.",
      "provenance": {
        "by": "runbook/book-record.workflow.js ext-v5, sonnet, 2026-10-21",
        "method": "page image"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "eb11c1-3:explanation-2",
      "type": "worked_example",
      "lo": "eb11c1-3:objective-2",
      "source_page": 15,
      "quote": "Change division to multiplication by using the reciprocal of the divisor.",
      "stem": "Calculate $\\frac{x^2-4x-5}{2x^2+5x+2}\\div\\frac{x^2-x-20}{2x^2-5x-3}$.",
      "solution": [
        "$\\frac{x^2-4x-5}{2x^2+5x+2}\\div\\frac{x^2-x-20}{2x^2-5x-3}$ (note: Change division to multiplication by using the reciprocal of the divisor.)",
        "$=\\frac{x^2-4x-5}{2x^2+5x+2}\\times\\frac{2x^2-5x-3}{x^2-x-20}$ (note: Factorise.)",
        "$=\\frac{(x+1)(x-5)}{(2x+1)(x+2)}\\times\\frac{(2x+1)(x-3)}{(x-5)(x+4)}$ (note: Cancel out common factors.)",
        "$=\\frac{(x+1)(x-3)}{(x+2)(x+4)}$ (note: Do not expand the brackets.)"
      ],
      "answer": "$\\frac{(x+1)(x-3)}{(x+2)(x+4)}$",
      "solution_provenance": "book_worked",
      "notes": "Explanation of Warm Up 2; cancelled factors (x-5) and (2x+1) are struck through in the image.",
      "provenance": {
        "by": "runbook/book-record.workflow.js ext-v5, sonnet, 2026-10-21",
        "method": "page image"
